Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: reserve an audio SSRC before the first offer

An SFU can decline the audio MID extension and demultiplex the stream by
its SDP SSRC. Create the audio identity with its outgoing source, retain
it across codec preferences and reuse it when packetizers are linked.
The initial track can still be null and later replaced without changing
the advertised SSRC.

--- a/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
@@ -1835,8 +1835,15 @@
     auto transactionId = createVersion4UUIDString();
     gst_structure_set(initData.get(), "transaction-id", G_TYPE_STRING, transactionId.ascii().data(), nullptr);

     GRefPtr<GstWebRTCRTPTransceiver> rtcTransceiver;
+    // Peers may decline the audio MID extension and associate RTP by SDP SSRC.
+    // Reserve that identity before the first offer, while the track is muted.
+    if (gst_caps_get_size(caps.get())) {
+        switchOn(source, [&](Ref<RealtimeOutgoingAudioSourceGStreamer>& audio) {
+            gst_structure_set(gst_caps_get_structure(caps.get(), 0), "ssrc", G_TYPE_UINT, audio->ssrc(), nullptr);
+        }, [](Ref<RealtimeOutgoingVideoSourceGStreamer>&) { }, [](std::nullptr_t&) { });
+    }
     g_signal_emit_by_name(m_webrtcBin.get(), "add-transceiver", direction, caps.get(), &rtcTransceiver.outPtr());
     if (!rtcTransceiver)
         return Exception { ExceptionCode::InvalidAccessError, "Unable to add transceiver"_s };

